{
  "_README": [
    "Hand-written. The ONE file in .brain/topics/ that is not generated.",
    "Extraction invents a fresh slug per dossier; this folds those into concepts.",
    "Deciding that two slugs name the same idea is editorial judgment — that is",
    "the whole point of the topic layer, and automating it would rebuild the",
    "sprawl it exists to fix. Slugs absent from here render as `provisional`,",
    "which is visible debt, not a silent guess. Rebuild with:",
    "  python -m tools.brain.topic_mine build",
    "Rules of thumb when adding: a concept must name a MECHANISM that could",
    "recur in a different episode. Never a person, document, place, or era.",
    "Reject vague catch-alls (`historical-context`, `biography`) — they carry no",
    "information and swallow claims that belong somewhere specific."
